{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merged: merge-path guidance that names its successors, on main at 8f22ba52.\n\nRetiring an artifact without naming what replaced it says \"gone\" where it means \"moved here\", and leaves a reader following the chain at a dead end holding prose no tool can resolve. The reference now reserves bare supersession for deletion alone, states that a successor is cited as a causal basis rather than described, and splits the rename case: renaming into an occupied path has two predecessors and one survivor.\n\nThe executable walkthrough keeps the merged artifact's EventID, passes it before the positional supersede target, and audits the survivor rather than the artifact it has just retired. The docset gate runs those commands rather than reading them, so the flag ordering is verified against the real binary.\n\nThe page-level lesson underneath all of it: a path is not a topic label, and a count in one page is a second copy of another page's table that can disagree with it. Both are stated where they bite.\n\nSuccessor at this path to 2b725f06, the reviewed branch artifact.","body":{"commit":"8f22ba52cbe5921127e767395eadf1f8eff0db52","path":"docs/reference/gs/merge.md"}}